-- title:
--   Taylor–Wiles modules over 𝒪[Δ_Q] in the flat minimal case
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero with finite residue field $k$, let $p\ne 2$ be a prime with $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$, and let $\bar\rho$ be an absolutely irreducible two-dimensional residual representation of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ over $k$. Let $\mathrm{Smin}\subseteq S$ be finite sets of primes with all members of $S$ prime, $p\in\mathrm{Smin}$, and, for $q\ne p$ prime, $q\in\mathrm{Smin}$ exactly when $\bar\rho$ is ramified at $q$; assume inertia at each $q\in\mathrm{Smin}$, $q\ne p$, acts on $\bar\rho$ with characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$. Let $N\ne 0$ be squarefree with all prime divisors in $S$, divisible by every $q\in\mathrm{Smin}\setminus\{p\}$, with every prime divisor other than $p$ in $\mathrm{Smin}$, and $p\nmid N$. Let $r\ge 5$ be a prime with $r\notin S$, $r\nmid Np$, $p\nmid r-1$, and $\mathrm{tr}\,\bar\rho(\sigma)^2\ne (r+1)^2$ for every Frobenius $\sigma$ at every place over $r$; assume weight-two cusp forms of level $\Gamma_0(N)$ are spanned over $\mathbb C$ by those with integral $q$-expansions. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the anemic Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) to $k$ with $\mathrm{charpoly}(\bar\rho(\sigma))=X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$ for all primes $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid N$ and all Frobenii at places over $\ell$, and let $H_n$ be a [`CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum`](def/CuspForm_HeckeGaloisRepDatum.html#L8) for $N,S,\mathcal O,\theta$ on the localisation $T=$ [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131): a map $\pi$ of the Hecke algebra into $T$ lifting $\theta$ residually, generating $T$ over $\mathcal O$, interpolating $\mathcal O$-valued characters lifting $\theta$, together with a Galois representation $\rho$ over $T$ whose Frobenius characteristic polynomials are $X^2-\pi(T_\ell)X+\ell$ and whose residual representation is absolutely irreducible. Let $L$ be a $T$-module which is finite and free over $\mathcal O$ (compatibly), let `hc` assert that the operators indexed by [`CuspForm.AuxLevel.Gen N r S`](def/CuspForm_AuxLevelHeckeModule.html#L11) (primes $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\ne r$) on the carrier [`CohCarrier.H1 (N * r) (subgroup N r) 𝒪`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L162) commute pairwise, and let $e_{ML}$ be an $\mathcal O$-linear isomorphism of $L$ with [`CuspForm.AuxLevel.ML N r S 𝒪 θ hc`](def/CuspForm_AuxLevelHeckeModule.html#L46) carrying the action of the image in $T$ of $T_\ell$ to the action of the polynomial variable indexed by the corresponding generator. Then for every $t$ and every injective $qv:\mathrm{Fin}\,t\to\mathbb N$ whose values are primes $\ge 5$ outside $S$ with $p\mid qv(i)-1$ and with $\bar\rho(\mathrm{Frob})$ having two distinct eigenvalues at each place over $qv(i)$, for every universal deformation datum $D_{\min}$ for the condition: cyclotomic determinant at $p$, finite flat at $p$, unramified outside $\mathrm{Smin}$, and unipotent on inertia at each $q\in\mathrm{Smin}$, $q\ne p$; for every universal deformation datum $D_Q$ for the same condition with ramification allowed at $\mathrm{Smin}\cup qv(\mathrm{Fin}\,t)$; for every local $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\varphi:D_{\min}.R\to T$ with $\varphi_*D_{\min}.\rho$ equivalent to $H_n.\rho$; and for all data $\mathrm{cyc}$ describing the Galois action on $q$-th roots of unity, surjections $\pi_\Delta$ of $(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ onto $\Delta_i=\mathbb Z/p^{v_p(q-1)}$ (for $q\ne p$), an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\varepsilon:D_Q.R\to D_{\min}.R$ which is local with $\varepsilon_*D_Q.\rho$ equivalent to $D_{\min}.\rho$, and an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\iota$ from $\mathcal O[\Delta_Q]$, $\Delta_Q=\prod_i\Delta_i$, into $D_Q.R$ killed by $\varepsilon$ on group elements with $\ker\varepsilon$ the ideal generated by the $\iota(g)-1$, such that for each $i$ inertia at each place over $qv(i)$ is diagonalised in some $D_Q.R$-basis of $D_Q.\rho.V$ by the characters $\iota\circ\pi_\Delta\circ\mathrm{cyc}$ in the $i$-th coordinate and its inverse: there exists a module $M_n$ over $D_Q.R$, over $\mathcal O[\Delta_Q]$ and over $\mathcal O$ compatibly, which is nontrivial, finite over $\mathcal O$, free over $\mathcal O[\Delta_Q]$, whose $\mathcal O[\Delta_Q]$-action is the restriction along $\iota$ of its $D_Q.R$-action, and an $\mathcal O$-linear isomorphism $e$ from the $\Delta_Q$-coinvariants $M_n/(\ker(\text{augmentation})\cdot M_n)$ onto $L$ with $e(\overline{x\cdot m})=\varphi(\varepsilon(x))\cdot e(\bar m)$ for all $x\in D_Q.R$.
--
--   This is the Hecke-theoretic half of the Taylor–Wiles argument in the case where $p$ does not divide the minimal level, so that the minimal deformation problem is finite flat at $p$: at each Taylor–Wiles level $Q=\{q_1,\dots,q_t\}$ it produces a module over the deformation ring $R_Q$ which is free over the group algebra $\mathcal O[\Delta_Q]$ and whose $\Delta_Q$-coinvariants recover, compatibly with the map $R_{\min}\to T$, the given Hecke module $L$ identified with the cohomology module at auxiliary level $r$. It feeds the assembly step [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_heckeModules_levelRaising_and_taylorWiles_auxLevel_of_isEis_kernel_pair_strictOrdinary_of_not_cube_dvd`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_heckeModules_levelRaising_and_taylorWiles_auxLevel_of_isEis_kernel_pair_strictOrdinary_of_not_cube_dvd), from which the patching argument and the modularity lifting theorem are deduced.
